  "content": {
    "id": "p96-task-tf",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p96-tf-instruction-text",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "True or False?",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p96-task-tf-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "If $y$ varies directly with $x$, then doubling the value of $x$ will double the value of $y$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "Direct variation gives $y=kx$. After doubling $x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=k(2x)\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=2kx\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=2y.\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p96-task-tf-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If $y$ varies directly with the square of $x$, then doubling the value of $x$ will double the value of $y$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False; $y$ quadruples.",
          "worked": "Here $y=kx^2$. After doubling $x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=k(2x)^2\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=4kx^2\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=4y.\\end{align*}$$\nFalse; $y$ quadruples.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p96-task-tf-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "If $y$ varies inversely with $x$, then tripling the value of $x$ will divide the value of $y$ by 3.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "Inverse variation gives $y=\\frac{k}{x}$. After tripling $x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{k}{3x}\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{k}{x}\\right)\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{y}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p96-task-tf-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "If $y$ varies inversely with the square of $x$, then halving $x$ will make $y$ one-quarter of its original value.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False; $y$ quadruples.",
          "worked": "Here $y=\\frac{k}{x^2}$. After halving $x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{k}{(x/2)^2}\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{4k}{x^2}\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=4y.\\end{align*}$$\nFalse; $y$ quadruples.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p96-task-tf-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "If $y$ varies directly with the square of $x$, then increasing $x$ by 10% increases $y$ by 21%.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "Here $y=kx^2$, and a $10\\%$ increase multiplies $x$ by $\\frac{11}{10}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=k\\left(\\frac{11}{10}x\\right)^2\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{121}{100}kx^2\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{121}{100}y.\\end{align*}$$\nThe multiplier is $1.21$, corresponding to a $21\\%$ increase. True.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p96-task-tf-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "If $y$ varies directly with the square root of $x$, then quadrupling $x$ will double $y$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "Here $y=k\\sqrt{x}$. After quadrupling $x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=k\\sqrt{4x}\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=2k\\sqrt{x}\\\\y_{\\mathrm{new}}&=2y.\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p96-task-tf-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "If $y$ varies inversely with $x$, and $x$ is negative, then $y$ must also be negative.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p96-task-tf-g-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "False.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p96-task-tf-g-short-reason",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For example, ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=-1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x=-1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " give ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Inverse variation gives $y=\\frac{k}{x}$, where $k\\ne0$. A negative value of $k$ is allowed. Take $k=-1$ and $x=-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{-1}{-1}\\\\y&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nFalse; negative $x$ does not force negative $y$. The sign also depends on $k$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p96-task-tf-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "Inverse variation results in a straight-line graph passing through the origin.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False; $y=\\frac{k}{x}$ is a hyperbola.",
          "worked": "Inverse variation has equation $y=\\frac{k}{x}$, with $k\\ne0$. Its graph is a hyperbola. Since $x=0$ is excluded, it cannot pass through the origin. False.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      }
    ]
  },
